R"VG(
# prehistoric.vg (H-04): the records of a people without writing: marks read as counts and pictures (the ideas note's section 9). The
# ship reads a bone's strokes, a painted wall's figures, a stone's signs: what is written here is its reading, a mark at a time,
# a count and what it counts. A person is a sign the marks repeat (the ship keeps their name as it keeps a name); nothing here
# writes, reads a page or cuts a lintel (the lexicon's medieval words). H-04's second pass: every people marks in its own way (the
# kind of strokes it cut, how it grouped them, the sign it drew for a beast, a birth, a death: `pre.*` pools, `people=K`), and the
# counts are of its own things (its game, its herd, its vessels, its crafts), so no two peoples' bones read alike.

# ---- how a people marked: its strokes, its grouping (each people its own few) ------------------------------------------------

pre.stroke (pl people=3)
  (medium=bone) notches
  (medium=bone) nicks
  (medium=bone) short cuts
  (medium=bone) deep cuts
  (medium=bone) slanting cuts
  (medium=bone) little crosses
  (medium=bone) paired notches
  (medium=stone) scratches
  (medium=stone) pecked dots
  (medium=stone) cup marks
  (medium=stone) short grooves
  (medium=stone) scratched crosses
  (medium=stone) ground rings
  (medium=painted) dots of paint
  (medium=painted) finger marks
  (medium=painted) painted strokes
  (medium=painted) thumb prints
  (medium=painted) short bars
  (medium=painted) red ticks
  strokes
  chevrons
  ticks

pre.groupby (people=1)
  grouped by {#number}, the way the {people} counted
  in hands of five
  each fifth one longer
  in pairs, like footprints
  with a gap after every {#number}
  each {#number:ord} one crossed
  in rows that turn back at the end
  in a spiral from the middle out
  in two rows, one above the other
  with a dot after every ten

# a group of marks, its number kept as .k for the line's meaning: `marks` leads a line (its grouping between commas), `marks.s` stands
# inside one (no clause)
marks
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke}
  (2) {n>.k} {pre.stroke}, set in a row,
  a row of {n>.k} {pre.stroke}
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke} in a row
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke}, some worn faint,
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke}, the last one deeper,
marks.s
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke}
  (2) {n>.k} {pre.stroke}
  a row of {n>.k} {pre.stroke}
  {n>.k} {pre.stroke} in a row
marksbig
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke}
  (2) {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke}, {pre.groupby},
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke}, packed close,
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke} in long rows
marksbig.s
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke}
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke} in long rows
  {nbig>.k} {pre.stroke} packed close

# where the marks stand against the sign
pre.by
  beside
  next to
  under
  over
  after
  around
  along

# ---- the signs a people drew for its things (each people its own two or three) ---------------------------------------------

pre.sign.game (people=2)
  a horned head
  a hoof
  an antler
  a track of two toes
  a running beast in three lines
  a spear point
  an eye with a line under it
  the head of a {game.one}
  a spear crossing a hoof
  a {game.one} drawn very small
pre.sign.fish (people=2)
  a fish
  a wavy line with a hook in it
  two crossed curves
  the diamond of a net
  a fish's tail
  a hook
  a fish with its mouth open
pre.sign.herd (people=2)
  a pair of horns
  a hoof
  a beast drawn very small
  a pen's circle with dots in it
  a tail and a back
  a {herd.sign}
herd.sign
  horned head
  hoof print
  young beast
  beast with its head down
pre.sign.moon (people=2)
  a filled circle
  a half circle
  a circle with a dot
  a ring of dots
  a circle cut through
  a crescent lying on its back
pre.sign.dead (people=2)
  a figure lying down
  a crossed stroke
  a closed eye
  a bowl turned over
  a hand with its fingers down
  a stroke ringed in {colour.mourn}
  a figure with its arms crossed
pre.sign.born (people=2)
  a small figure
  a small figure held up
  a circle inside a circle
  two hands round a dot
  a seed with a line from it
  a figure with a small one on its back
pre.sign.rain (people=2)
  a wavy line
  falling dots
  a cloud with lines under it
  a bowl filling
  three hanging lines
pre.sign.sun (people=2)
  a sun with rays
  a circle with long rays
  a cracked line
  an open hand turned up
  a circle with a dot at its middle
pre.sign.hunger (people=2)
  an empty bowl
  a closed hand
  a belly drawn hollow
  a bowl turned over
  a figure with its ribs drawn
pre.sign.band (people=2)
  the sign of another band
  a hand of a different shape
  a figure with a strange head
  two lines crossing
  a circle with a line through it
pre.sign.walk (people=2)
  a line with a circle at each end
  a line of footprints
  a path drawn in dots
  a line with knots in it
  a line that bends round a hill

# ---- the counts: the sign, the marks, what they count ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# a count's shape: the marks by the sign, or the sign first; `.k` the count, kept for the meaning
count.game
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.game}: {pre.cnt.game}.
  {pre.sign.game}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.game}.
  {marks.s}, then {pre.sign.game}: {pre.cnt.game}.
  (medium!=painted) {pre.sign.game} with {marks.s} cut through it: {pre.cnt.game}.
  Under {pre.sign.game}, {marks.s}: {pre.cnt.game}.
pre.cnt.game
  {.k} {game} {count.taken}
  {.k} {game}, {count.taken} {count.when}
  the hunt, {.k} {game}
  {.k} {game} {count.taken}, and the meat shared
  {.k} {game} {count.taken} {count.where.at}
  {.k} {game}, and one more crossed out
count.fish
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.fish}: {pre.cnt.fish}.
  {pre.sign.fish}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.fish}.
  {marks.s}, then {pre.sign.fish}: {pre.cnt.fish}.
pre.cnt.fish
  {.k} days of {fish}
  the water gave {.k} {vessel} of {fish}
  {.k} days at the water, {count.when}
  {.k} {vessel} of {fish}, dried
  {.k} {vessel} of {fish}, {count.when}
count.herd
  {marksbig} {pre.by} {pre.sign.herd}: {pre.cnt.herd}.
  {pre.sign.herd}, and {marksbig.s} after it: {pre.cnt.herd}.
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.herd}: {pre.cnt.herdyoung}.
  {pre.sign.herd}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.herdyoung}.
pre.cnt.herd
  the {herd}, {.k} of them
  {.k} {herd}
  the {herd} of {$home}, {.k}
  {.k} {herd} taken up to the high ground
  {.k} {herd} driven home {count.when}
pre.cnt.herdyoung
  {.k} young, born {count.when}
  {.k} young ones, and two dead
  {.k} {herd} born
  the increase, {.k}
count.hunger
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.hunger}: {pre.cnt.hunger}.
  {pre.sign.hunger}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.hunger}.
pre.cnt.hunger
  {.k} days of hunger
  {.k} days with nothing in the {vessel}
  {.k} days on {fuel} smoke and water
  {.k} days before the {game} came
  {.k} days of eating the seed
count.moon
  {pre.sign.moon}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.moon}.
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.moon}: {pre.cnt.moon}.
  {marks.s} between two of {pre.sign.moon.pl}: {pre.cnt.moon}.
pre.sign.moon.pl
  the filled circles
  the half circles
  the rings
  the crescents
pre.cnt.moon
  {.k} full moons
  {.k} turns of the moon {count.when}
  the moon's turn, {.k} nights
  {.k} nights from one full moon to the next
  {.k} moons since the {herd} went up
count.lost
  {marks.s}, crossed through, {pre.by} {pre.sign.dead}: {pre.cnt.lost}.
  {pre.sign.dead}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.lost}.
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.dead}: {pre.cnt.lost}.
pre.cnt.lost
  {.k} who did not come back
  {.k} dead, {count.when}
  {.k} gone {count.where.at}
  (cold=1) {.k} lost on the ice
  {.k} who went to {deadplace}
count.born
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.born}: {pre.cnt.born}.
  {pre.sign.born}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.born}.
pre.cnt.born
  {.k} children born
  {.k} born, {count.when}
  {.k} born and {.k} living, which is luck
  {.k} children, the year's
  {.k} born in {house.one}
count.rain
  {pre.sign.rain}, and {marks.s} after it: {.k} days of rain.
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.rain}: {.k} days of rain {count.when}.
  {pre.sign.sun}, and {marks.s} after it: {.k} days without rain.
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.sun}: {.k} days of {weather.now}.
count.trade
  {marks} {pre.by} {pre.sign.band}: {pre.cnt.trade}.
  {pre.sign.band}, and {marks.s} after it: {pre.cnt.trade}.
  (3 contact=1) {marks} {pre.by} a sign that is not theirs, the {other}'s: {.k} {trade.thing} traded.
pre.cnt.trade
  {.k} {trade.thing} given to them, and a line drawn back for what came in return
  {.k} {trade.thing} for their {material}
  {.k} {trade.thing}, owed
  {.k} {trade.thing} for a {beast} and its young
  {.k} {trade.thing} given at the gathering
count.walk
  {marks.s} along {pre.sign.walk}: {.k} days' walk between {$home} and {count.where}.
  {pre.sign.walk}, and {marks.s} along it: {.k} days to {count.where}.
  {marks.s} along {pre.sign.walk}, and a fire drawn at the end: {.k} nights out, to {count.where}.
count.make
  {marks} {pre.by} the sign for {tool}: {.k} {pre.made}.
  {marks} {pre.by} the sign for {vessel}: {.k} {pre.made}.
  {marks.s} under a hand holding {tool}: {.k} days of {craft}.

pre.made
  made
  made and given away
  finished before the snow
  made by one hand, by the look of them
  made, two broken

trade.thing (pl people=3)
  skins
  flints
  {vessel}
  shells
  beads
  furs
  blades
  baskets of salt
  {fruit}
  ochre cakes
  fish hooks

count.taken (people=4)
  taken
  brought home
  killed
  driven over the edge
  taken with the nets
  taken in the pits
  run down by the dogs
  speared
  trapped
  (cold=1) taken in the snow
  (desert=1) taken at the dry pools
  (coast=1) taken on the rocks

count.when (people=5)
  in {season.now}
  after the long night
  in the time of the {crop2}
  when the {bird} came back
  when {river} was low
  at {festival}
  before the {herd} went up
  in the moon of the {game}
  when the {tree} were bare
  (cold=1) before the snow
  (cold=1) in the deep cold
  (desert=1) in the dry months
  (desert=1) after the dust
  (moons>0) under a new {moon}

count.where
  the water
  the hills
  {mountain}
  {river}
  the camp of the old ones
  the flint place
  (coast=1) the shore
  (desert=1) the dry pools
count.where.at
  at the ford
  in the hills
  under {mountain}
  by {river}
  at the far water
  (coast=1) on the shore
  on the way back

# ---- the object itself: its state, as the ship finds it ---------------------------------------------------------------------

obj.state
  {obj.part} {obj.how}.
  {obj.part} {obj.how}; {obj.more}.
  {obj.part} {obj.how}, and {obj.how2}.
  {obj.more.cap}.
pre.wrap (people=2)
  hide
  bark
  reed matting
  felt
  a {garment.n}
  {colour.holy} cloth
obj.part
  The end of it
  The back
  The last mark
  The edge
  The underside
  One corner
  The oldest mark
  The middle
  The flat side
  The worn end
obj.how
  is worn smooth where it was held
  is broken off
  is stained with {colour.holy}
  is scorched, as if it was kept near a fire
  is cut over older marks
  is polished, as if rubbed for luck
  has a hole bored through it, for a cord
  is chipped, and the chip is lost
  is darker than the rest
  is gnawed by something small
  is cracked along the grain
obj.how2
  the cord is long gone
  someone has tried to mend it
  the rest is clean
  the ship can read only half
  it was put back where it was found
obj.more
  someone kept it in {vessel.one} for a long time
  whoever cut the last marks meant to come back
  a hand is pressed in {colour.holy} beside them
  it lay under the floor of {house.one}
  it was wrapped in {pre.wrap}, and the wrapping has rotted
  someone cut a small face there, smiling, or the ship reads it so
  the marks there are fresher
  a child's marks are mixed in with the rest
  the ship cannot say what the last sign means, a thing like {pre.eye.like}
  it was found with {tool} and a string of beads
  {motif.over} the {people} put on everything are cut along its back
  it smells of {fuel} smoke still
obj.more.cap
  It was found with others like it, in a pit by the hearth, under {fuel} ash
  It was found under the floor of {house.one}
  It lay in {vessel.one} with {tool} and a handful of beads
  It was buried with care, wrapped in {pre.wrap}
  The {pre.stroke} at the end are fresher than the rest
  The ship cannot say what the last sign means; it looks like {pre.eye.like}
  A child has scratched {motif.over} along the edge
)VG"
